                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There are better things you can do with your money. \r\n\r\nEternity The Last Unicorn is basically an old school combat driven explorer puzzle game where you do mostly fighting, light puzzling, and experience some basic unvoiced storytelling.\r\n\r\nSounds fine right? Sure, but the combat isn't that fun. In the beginning, you REALLY need to dodge and place your attacks well, again, sounds fine, but enemies can end you fairly quickly right at the start. With minimal items, it's not a great experience. Moreso, the rune item type is very expensive, so much so that you'd think they were permanent bonuses.\r\n\r\nOver time, you'll unlock the ability to upgrade your weapons, and you'll find items that upgrade your maximum health. This does make the game easier, but I'd compare it to pouring your favorite topping on your least favorite food. Some hot sauce isn't going to help it as much as it needs. \r\n\r\nEven further in, you'll unlock another weapon for both characters. Sounds good again right? This weapon is mainly for removing the \"Invincible until you hit me with THAT weapon\" mechanic. Turning what used to be bad Dynasty Warriors combat spam, into a staggering, throttled experience of trying to hit practically invincible enemies instead of the standard fodder. I say practically invincible because if you use your stored \"ultimate move\" it deals damage to them, if you can defeat them with that, it'll save you the trouble, but it takes defeating enemies or sustaining damage to charge. It's an option. The elf character can break this invincible aura with one shot, however, the warrior needs 3 hits of his slow unwieldy weapon to do the same.\r\n\r\nThe story is pretty bare. So you're essentially suffering through the above to get what would otherwise be a text based generic fan fiction, more like a template for you to add details yourself so it isn't that bad.\r\n\r\nAt the end of the day it feels like those old unity asset early access games that \"just need a little more funding\" to be better, but it's an unreal engine game. It usually doesn't.\r\n\r\nBut hey, relatively easy achievements I guess. Though I'm sure there are much better games ,or much cheaper games to do this with.",
